===Roles===
When in the Theatre, experienced players choose one of three roles, which affects the gear/spellbook they will bring into the raid. Learners should bring the most basic items to cover all three roles, with their remaining inventory slots being used for supplies instead of gear switches.

Below is a simplified summary of the roles as they appear in a 4-Scale:
* Meleer ("mdps") - uses the [[Arceuus spellbook]] ([[thralls]]), uses a 3-tick or multi-hit melee weapon during the nylocas waves (on the western side of the arena).
* Ranger ("rdps") - uses the [[Lunar spellbook]] ([[Boost Potion Share]] and [[Vengeance]]), uses the blowpipe and chinchompas during the nylocas waves.
* Freezer - uses [[Ancient Magicks]] ([[Ice Barrage]] and [[Blood Barrage]]), split into two types:
** Melee freezer/north freezer ("mfrz"/"nfrz") - freezes the north 1, north 2, and all 3 and 4 nylocas at Maiden (3s and 4s are the nylocas which spawn on the eastern side of the arena, and will clump together 11 ticks and 16 ticks after spawning, respectively) . Mainly uses melee during the nylocas waves (on the eastern side of the arena), but can also use magic if necessary.
** Mage/south freezer ("mage"/"sfrz") - freezes the south 1 and south 2 nylocas (and should be prepared to freeze all 4s if necessary, e.g. if nfrz is late) at Maiden. Uses only magic during the nylocas waves.

==Bosses==
The Theatre of Blood is a linear raid. Thus, there is no randomisation involved, and the bosses will always be encountered in this order.

The raid can be done in a team of up to five players, with the enemies' health scaling accordingly to the size. Enemies have their health adjusted to a five-man encounter, but will be lowered to 87.5% in 4-man encounters and 75.0% in trio and lower scales. It is possible to duo the raid, but this is mostly done for the [[Theatre (Duo) Speed-Runner]] [[Combat Achievement]] task.

In all of the rooms before Verzik, a barrier separates the team from the boss, and the fight only begins once a player has crossed the barrier, meaning it is possible for a player to avoid some fights in larger groups. However, this will impact overall drops and is not recommended in most cases.

Each boss has a health bar displayed at the top of the screen in percent, giving a rough estimate as to how much health it has left. The only exception is the Nylocas build-up waves, which is the health of the four pillars in the room.
#[[The Maiden of Sugadinti]] (level-940)
#[[Pestilent Bloat]] (level-870)
#[[Nylocas Vasilias]] (level-800)
#[[Sotetseg]] (level-995)
#[[Xarpus]] (level-960)
#[[Verzik Vitur]] (level-1040, final boss)
