==The Nylocas==
[[File:Fighting Nylocas hordes.png|thumb|A group of players battle against the Nylocas hordes.]]
The [[Nylocas]] are found in the third room of the Theatre of Blood.

Before starting the room, sip a dose of stamina potion and repot combat potions if necessary. Generally, the ranger should share a stamina potion via [[Stat Restore Pot Share]] before starting the waves.

Each player should be assigned a style of Nylocas to kill prior to starting the room. The assigned roles depend on team size:
* 5-Scale: x2 magers, x2 melee, x1 ranger
* 4-Scale: x1 mager, x2 melee, x1 ranger
* Trio: x1 mager, x1 melee, x1 ranger

One player, ideally a ranger, should use [[Boost Potion Share]] on a [[stamina potion]] as there is a lot of running in the nylocas waves, especially for melee users. 

Meleers with a scythe are encouraged to bring another weapon for this room, such as [[Dual macuahuitl]]s, though [[Glacial temotli]]s or [[Sulphur blades]] are an acceptable substitute. Multi-hit weapons will make as many rolls as possible, which can easily overkill nylos with good strength bonus. Since small nylocas are 1x1, using a scythe on them is discouraged unless they are lined up in a manner that the scythe can hit several at once or against a large nylocas. As these weapons are easily accessible and very cheap, these should be used by all melee players regardless of their melee armour used. While 3-tick weapons such as a [[ham joint]] or [[swift blade]] can perform better than the 4-tick weapon, this requires no wasted ticks (which is highly unlikely) and an additional inventory space to slot a defender to maximise strength bonus.

Rangers should use a [[toxic blowpipe]] in this room. Chinchompas can help deal with clusters of nylocas, but this is only needed if teams are struggling to kill them.

Mages should use an [[eye of ayak]], as its 3 tick speed and fairly high damage makes clearing them incredibly trivial. If not available, use a 4 tick staff instead, although this will result in more leaks. Barrages should only be used when the fight becomes hectic. Frozen nylocas will usually stop attacking a pillar for a short time.

As the nylocas have nonexistent defence bonuses (including the Hagios, who have no Magic), players are encouraged to focus on strength bonus over accuracy.

===Waves overview===
The fight starts off with 31 waves of Nylocas [[Nylocas Toxobolos|Toxobolos]] (green), [[Nylocas Hagios|Hagios]] (blue) and [[Nylocas Ischyros|Ischyros]] (grey) from the tunnels. Each spider is immune to damage outside of their combat style - ranged must be used against the Toxobolos, magic against the Hagios, and melee against the Ischyros. If the nylocas is attacked with a wrong style, the player that attacked them can no longer damage them.

The goal is to kill all the Nylocas before all four [[Support (Theatre of Blood)|pillars]] are [[Broken support|destroyed]] (as indicated by their health bar; the green health bar at the top is the overall health of all four). If a pillar is broken, it will collapse and deal up to 50 damage to the entire team. If the nylocas manage to break all four pillars, the team will be instantly killed.

[[File:The Nylocas - melee role showcase.mp4|thumb|400px|A demonstration of a player in the melee role, with a swift blade to hit faster and the Scythe of Vitur to hit multiple Ischyros.]]
The nylocas waves are not randomised. It is highly recommended to pick a role and memorise the waves to make the room easier. Magers and rangers should prioritise killing clumps of nylocas with barrage and chinchompas, and meleers should help the mager while they move to the next melee nylocas.

There are two sizes of nylocas - a level 162 variant with 11 health (9 in 4-Scale, 8 in trios), a max hit of 17, and occupying a 1x1 tile. There is also a level 260 variant with 22 health (19 in 4-Scale, 16 in trios), a max hit of 24, and occupying a 2x2 tile. When the large nylocas is killed, they will spawn two smaller nylocas of any type.

Most of the nylocas will focus on attacking the pillars, but a few will not do so and attack the team instead. They are the same as nylocas walking into the arena, but will stop slightly before they attack the team. These "aggro's" should be prioritised first as they can hit quite hard and distract the team from the ones breaking the pillars. Starting from wave 16, some of the nylocas will begin to "flicker", swapping between combat styles in a pre-determined pattern. If player makes an attack just before the nylocas changes forms, they will still take damage from it.

Using the RuneLite plugin '''Better NPC Highlight''' helps easily identify the aggressive nylocas, and is recommended so players can immediately react to them:

*Small melee: 8348
*Large melee: 8351
*Small range: 8349
*Large range: 8352
*Small magic: 8350
*Large magic: 8353

It is important to kill the nylocas as fast as possible, as the next wave will be stalled; between waves 1-19, up to 12 nylocas can be active before waves are paused. After wave 20, this cap is raised to 24 nylocas. Having many nylocas active at once will result in a quicker pillar loss, so try to kill them as quickly as possible.

Nylocas will self-destruct 30 seconds after spawning; small nylocas can deal up to 18 damage, while larger ones can deal up to 21. This is more of a concern for melee players, since the exploding nylocas will always be near supports. As such, try to always kill newly spawned nylocas after dealing with aggro's, prioritising the smaller ones first. Lastly, '''always''' be on the attack; if your assigned nylocas are not currently near or in the room, switch weapons (and some gear, if killing mage nylocas as melee) until the assigned nylocas return.
{{Otheruses|def=no|a full overview of the nylocas waves|Theatre of Blood/Strategies/Nylocas}}
===Nylocas Vasilias===
[[File:Fighting Nylocas Vasilias.png|thumb|A group of players fighting the Nylocas Vasilias, a result of Verzik Vitur's diverse breeding program.]]
After the 31 waves of nylocas are cleared, a [[Nylocas Vasilias]] will drop down from the middle of the room as the final enemy. During this brief interlude, the team should heal up and boost. In larger scales, you may group together to allow the ranger to use [[Boost Potion Share]] on a ranging potion.

The player should '''always''' switch protection prayers to '''Protect from Melee''' before attacking, as the Nylocas Vasilias can hit up to 70 off-prayer, and 17 if prayed against (except melee, which is fully protected). When its form changes, the player should again switch prayers. As its defences are pitiful, players getting to grips with the raid may opt to switch less gear without much drawback due to the short time it stays in one form. The boss will change forms every 10 ticks (6 seconds) to another form that it is not currently using. This is equal to 2 attacks from a 4/5-tick weapon, 3 from a 3-tick weapon and 4 from a 2-tick weapon. The player will stop attacking when Vasilias changes forms.

Vasilias will always spawn in its melee form. One player should use a Bandos godsword special to reduce its Defence, since it only has 50 Defence with no defence bonuses, with the other players dumping dragon claws or crystal halberd specials. Just like the waves of nylocas before, the boss is immune to damage of the wrong combat style. However, attacking it with the incorrect style will result in the player taking damage they would have dealt to it, and healing it for the same amount.

