==Sotetseg==
[[File:Fighting Sotetseg.png|thumb|A group of players battle against Sotetseg, a dark beast corrupted through Haemalchemy and experiments in the [[Shadow Realm]].]]
[[Sotetseg]] is a large dark beast imbued with blood through Haemalchemy, and the fourth boss in the Theatre of Blood.

Before starting the fight, special attack roles are assigned to players to drain its Defence: 1-2, 1-3, 2-3, and backup. The number indicates when the player will use a special attack; the backup is incase one of the player(s) misses:
* 1 - upon starting the fight
* 2 - upon clearing the first maze (after 66.6% health)
* 3 - upon clearing the second maze (after 33.3% health)

===Attacks===
Sotetseg attacks with both melee and magic. The melee attack consists of a lunge with its horns that can deal up to 45 damage (22 if prayed against), while the magic attack is a small red projectile. When the magic projectile is launched at his main target, it will split up to two additional projectiles upon impact, which can be either a magic (red) or ranged (black) projectile. 

The projectiles will deal [[successful hit]]s of up to 50 damage and disable protection prayers, but are fully blocked if prayed against correctly. As such, having the correct prayers active is vital as it may lead to a swift death if multiple projectiles are targeting the player in a short period of time. If hit, step away from Sotetseg to avoid the chance of a melee attack while you recover. These projectiles are small and can be hard to spot, especially when they travel through the boss, so some players opt for plugins to change its appearance.

Due to this attack, teams will position themselves at various spots around Sotetseg to increase the projectile's travel time so they can be reacted to in time. In a trio encounter, players will stand to the east, west and north-west respectively. In 4-man encounters, each player will stand in the corresponding corner for that row/column. In 5-man encounters, one player will also stand to the south-centre tile.
[[File:Sotetseg - tick eating.mp4|thumb|400px|To tick-eat the red ball, click on your food right as the second attack animation starts.]]

After 10 magic attacks, Sotetseg will launch a massive red ball at one player, indicated with the message "[Player name] has discovered a large ball of energy coming their way..." The damage scales to group size and players present in the arena (not dead). If two or more players are present in the arena, the ball is guaranteed to kill the targeted player, as it will deal 121+ damage onto them. This damage can be split among other players to safer amounts.

It is possible to [[tick eat]] the red ball, allowing the team to maintain their normal formation, but this is only recommended if some players are critically low on health, since players can risk getting combo'ed by an incoming projectile. To tick eat the attack, players must eat immediately after Sotetseg's second attack animation starts.

===Shadow maze===
At 66.6% and 33.3% health, Sotetseg will choose one player to pull into the Shadow Realm, indicated with a bright white light and the message {{mes|Sotetseg chooses you...}}. The remaining players will be forcibly teleported to the other end of the arena instead; incoming attacks made by Sotetseg, including the big red ball, will not deal damage.

The player in the Shadow Realm will be presented with a randomly generated path leading to a portal on the other side. While in the Shadow Realm, the player will take 1 to 3 damage every 7 ticks (4.2 seconds). When the grid is stepped on, players in the real world will see the tile the player in the Shadow Realm is standing on with a red glow.
[[File:Sotetseg - maze running.mp4|thumb|400px|A player runs through the Shadow Realm maze without damaging their teammates in the real world.]]
The maze runner should stop on the third row and wait a few seconds to let their teammates position themselves. Once someone steps on the fourth row, a tornado will spawn that will follow the maze path and deal massive damage to anyone caught in it. If a player accidentally steps on the fourth row, they can quickly move back to the third to despawn it. This tornado will not appear for the maze runner (unless they are the only player in the encounter). If the wrong tile is stepped on, then a blast will emit from the tile, dealing damage to nearby players equal to 6.67% of the player's current [[Hitpoints]] + 15 every tick, so it is important not to run into the wrong tile, as this will quickly kill the entire team.

Advanced players can use diagonal and L movements to skip over few tiles off the correct path; the tiles '''cannot''' be run skipped. Players can use [https://devqhp.github.io/osrs/sotetseg/ this external tool] to practice maze running, which simulates the game's movement mechanics; to get a maze identical to the clip, click "Edit Seed" at the bottom right and enter <code>7 10 12 11 12 7 11 12</code>.

After clearing the maze, Sotetseg's Defence level is restored, necessitating further Defence-draining special attacks by players based on their assigned special attack order.

Once Sotetseg is slain, the last and final supply chest will be available to the team. Make use of any partial potions and buy full ones with the points allotted to them. Inexperienced team should buy as many brews and restores as possible along with one stamina potion. Experienced teams can expect to have 2-3 brews and restores, while one player buys another stamina potion to be used for Verzik to share with the others.

