==Xarpus==
[[File:Fighting Xarpus.png|thumb|A group of players fighting Xarpus, the last of the Yarasa race and its king.]]
[[Xarpus]] is the last of the Yarasa, a race feared by the [[vampyre]]s, and is the fifth boss in the Theatre of Blood.

Upon entering the room, raiders should drop some potions to make room for any two-handed weapons they will be using during the fight. Generally no supplies should be used in this room.

===Phase 1===
Xarpus is significantly weakened at the start of the fight, starting with 75% of his health but does not attack players. During the first half, he will unearth [[exhumed]] skeletons and absorb the launched projectiles to heal himself for a percentage of his health; 12 exhumed in trios, 9 in 4-man and 6 in 5-man scales. 

To prevent the exhumed from healing Xarpus, players simply need to stand on top of them until they return to the ground. The exhumed will spawn at a fast rate, especially in 4/5-man encounters to the point that it is not possible to completely prevent them from healing him even slightly. They will spawn everywhere across the arena, and players are recommended to stand in the centre of the arena to quickly intercept any exhumed that appear. After 15 exhumed have been exhausted (12 in trio), Xarpus will initiate the next phase of the fight. All players should have their defence-draining weapon equipped, and melee players should activate [[Redemption]].

===Phase 2===
Xarpus has a high Defence level of 250, with ranged defences of +160 across the board. This makes it a make-or-break scenario depending on how many Defence levels were drained from him. The team should have at least two successful hammer/maul specials before draining the remaining Defence with godsword specials.

Upon starting phase 2, Xarpus will spit poison at players, whom are targeted based on orb order. The poison will splatter in one tile but has a 3x3 AoE which can inflict poison starting at 2 damage; standing on, running over, or being in the splatter's AoE will deal up to 8 poison damage per tick. The hit is slightly delayed if run over. The first player will splatter to the next player in sequence, while the remaining players will splatter to the next two players in sequence.

In the event that all players are on the same tile, or only one person is present in the arena, the poison will splatter a random uncovered tile. He also has a stomp attack where he rapidly throws pebbles dealing up to 9 damage per tick if a player is standing under him. This will interrupt his poison attack.

====Using melee====
[[File:Xarpus - melee with Scythe of Vitur.mp4|thumb|400px|A player melees Xarpus with the Scythe of Vitur; the key is to always run back once you see or hear him attack.]]
As Xarpus has no melee defence, it is encouraged to learn how to melee Xarpus if a scythe is in the player's possession to significantly decrease kill times. Melee Xarpus requires some practice and skill in ensuring that the poison will not splatter on a tile next to him, especially the marked tiles as shown in the image, as splattering these are detrimental to the team. Melee players should have [[Redemption]] on to circumvent the poison's low damage, as it can never kill the player at 90+ Hitpoints. If players are ranging, stand on the back two rows to give the melee users space.

Melee users can preemptively step back for 1 tick when Xarpus attacks with poison. If on the correct timing, no poison will splatter next to the boss and players can melee every cycle with a 4 tick weapon (Whip or Saeldor). With a 5 tick weapon (Scythe or Soulreaper axe), players will only delay an attack once in their cycle. This uses 15/16 available ticks to damage the boss, or effectively a 5.33 tick attack speed.

To remove this extra delay and attack every 5 ticks, players will have to intentionally rag a tile next to Xarpus every 4th hit. It can be any tile as long as it is not the highlighted tiles for Phase 3. Previously ragged tiles can be reused as many times as needed as long as the player has enough health.

===Phase 3===
[[File:Xarpus Melee tiles.png|thumb|Tiles that can be used to melee Xarpus without wasting ticks. The outer layer is for phase 2. The inner layer is for phase 3, safe tiles that can be used to run under Xarpus and poison splatters without taking damage.]]

Upon reaching ~25% of his health, Xarpus will screech, halting all poison attacks as he begins to stare at a quadrant intensely. He will rotate every 8 ticks afterwards to look at another corner. If a player attacks from a corner that Xarpus is looking at, he will retaliate back with an unblockable poison hit dealing 50-80 damage for each hitsplat; essentially, using weapons that hit two or more times as part of its attack will likely result in instant death.

Xarpus will never look in the same corner twice, so players should be moving to where he last looked if possible. Since he turns every 8 ticks, this equates to 2 hits from a 4-tick weapon, 4 from a 2-tick weapon and 1/2 from a 5-tick weapon (1 attack on one quadrant then 2 on another). If the team did not rag the primary tiles (which should hopefully be the case), the team can navigate through them with a diagonal run to a desired quadrant without taking damage.

Once Xarpus is defeated, pick up dropped supplies (if any were dropped) and have a team member grab the [[Dawnbringer]] before proceeding to the final boss of the raid.

