==Verzik Vitur - phase 1==
[[File:Verzik Tiles.png|thumb|Some recommended tiles to use at Verzik. The first two at the top are for melee, with the next two below them pillar safespots from the magic attack. The cluster of tiles in the centre are for melee'ing Verzik in phase 2. The tiles marked A to D are tiles for meleeing Verzik when she uses her web attack in phase 3.]]
Before starting the fight, players should drop 1-2 brews and restores where they intend to stand during phase 2. In the event of a disconnection or an early death, the potions will be available for other raiders to use.

'''All players must have Protect from Magic on before starting the fight.'''

During phase 1, Verzik has a shield around her to protect her from incoming damage, [[Maximum damage cap|capping damage]] dealt to her with melee at 10, with ranged and magic at 3.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1038039719437848576|date=7 September 2018|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/9KLSn|archivedate=1 September 2023|quote=Sorry, I must have misread it last time. It's 10 for melee, 3 for magic and ranged.}}

The [[Dawnbringer]] is the lone exception, which also ignores [[Magic#Magic_accuracy|accuracy rolls]], meaning the player will always deal [[successful hit]]s, even when at or below -64 Magic attack bonus. Additionally, its special attack deals 75-150 magic damage against her shield (average of 112.5 damage per special attack), thus requiring players to drop the Dawnbringer for the next player (in orb order) to use.

Additionally, every 14 ticks (8.4 seconds), Verzik will charge a magic attack that can deal up to 137 damage, which cannot be tick-eaten. Having [[Protect from Magic]] active before the projectile is launched will reduce the damage by 50%, or 68 damage. If the player is safely behind a [[Supporting Pillar]], the pillar will take the attack instead. As long as one player hides behind the pillar before the attack is launched, it will take damage, and multiple players hiding behind a pillar will only deal one instance of damage to it. When the pillar's health reaches 0, it will collapse, dealing heavy damage to anyone next to it when it collapses, pushing them a few tiles away and stunning them.

===Strategy===
[[File:Verzik Vitur - phase 1 movements.mp4|thumb|400px|A demonstration of the precise timing required to squeeze in two attacks between her magic attacks, as well as the movements between pillars.]]
In this phase, Verzik has her Defence lowered to 20. Due to the damage cap applied during this phase, players should use their melee weapons. Since the damage cap is per hitsplat, weapons that hit several times are recommended for this phase.

Spam-click Verzik so that you immediately attack when the team leader starts the fight. The player can safely attack four times with a 4-tick weapon, or 3 times with a 5-tick weapon. Afterwards, hide behind one pillar together, as the magic attack will be launched each pillar that is hiding a player. Verzik will proceed to charge the attack every 14 ticks (8.4 seconds) afterwards, which allows for two hits by any 4 or 5-tick weapon before requiring to hide behind a pillar.

The team should hide behind the pillar directly south-west of Verzik, then move east once the right one collapses. Regardless of team size, this phase should ideally end before the second pillar collapses. Once Verzik's shield has shattered, she will leave her throne, causing all remaining pillar supports to collapse, so players should stay away from them.

The simplest approach to this phase, "416" or "pillar drop", is to simply drop the Dawnbringer behind the pillar, however this is not optimal. More advanced teams will drop the Dawnbringer at Verzik's throne, or even tank her attacks entirely, to avoid losing out on ticks that could have been used to attack the boss. This should be discussed and agreed upon between the team ''before'' initiating phase 1 if at all possible. 

{{Recommended equipment
| style = Verzik P1
| weapon1 = {{plink|Scythe of vitur}}
| weapon2 = {{plink|Dual macuahuitl}} > {{plink|Sulphur blades}}
| weapon3 = {{plink|Blade of Saeldor}} / {{plink|Abyssal tentacle}} / {{plink|Noxious halberd}}
}}
{{Notelist}}

==Verzik Vitur - phase 2==
[[File:Fighting Verzik Vitur.png|thumb|A group of players fighting Verzik Vitur, now hoisted on a harness.]]
Verzik will fly from her throne to the middle of the room, with increased health and raising her Defence level to 200. The other stats remain the same. Defence-draining special attacks will have no effect, noted by the game message {{mes|Verzik Vitur absorbs the defence reduction!}}.

During phase 2, players should pray [[Protect from Missiles]], split up, and move to opposite sides of Verzik.
* 5-Scale: two go east, two go west, one goes south
* 4-Scale: two go east, and two go west
* Trios: one goes south, one east, and one west
Maintain this formation for the entirety of this phase, as this maintains space for urnbombs, lightning and the AoE heal.

Verzik will primarily attack with ranged during the start of this phase, throwing urnbombs at all players' current locations when the attack is used. These are [[successful hit]]s that deal up to 44 damage (22 with [[Protect from Missiles]]), but can be dodged by simply avoiding the tile the urn was thrown at. The damage is calculated on impact. As such, it is possible to save a few prayer points by not activating Protect from Missiles, though players who have high ping should not attempt this.

If any players are within melee range, there is a very high chance for her to do a body slam instead, dealing up to 45 damage to one of them, rolling against crush defence and knocking them back three tiles. This also stuns them for 3 seconds exposing the player to an urnbomb. If players stand underneath Verzik, she may yell {{overhead|There's nothing for you there!}} and deal up to 82 stomp damage, also knocking the player away. Unlike the body slam, the stomp attack is always a successful hit.; [[Protect from Melee]] has no effect on both attacks.

Every five attacks, Verzik will fire a ball of lightning, bouncing between players up to four times. If the lightning passes through Verzik, she will be hit for 15-20 damage.{{CiteTwitter|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1311663954251313153|author=Mod Ash|date=30 July 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/105970|archivedate=18 January 2022|quote=15-20. No accuracy calculation.}} As such, maintaining the aforementioned formation is key, as being too far from teammates will result in the lightning hitting you for up to 48 damage (25 if wearing [[insulated boots]]). If the lightning bounces 4 times without passing through Verzik, it also deals up to 48 damage to that player.

{{Bug|The damage dealt by the lightning ball will not be capped in Normal Mode if there is only one player left alive in a team of multiple people.}}

[[File:Verzik Vitur - phase 2 melee.mp4|thumb|400px|A demonstration of the timing required to safely melee Verzik with a whip/Scythe.]]
To dodge urnbombs and the slam attack, players must step back to a different tile or by stepping back before the scan tick where she determines whether to bomb or slam you. To effectively use a [[Scythe of vitur]] during phase 2, you must use the latter method, which is commonly referred to as "Scythe walking".

To scythe walk, you must be next to Verzik for all 3 safe ticks; the visual cue to click back is when the urnbomb explodes on the ground. As soon as it explodes click back, then click back on Verzik, done right your character should never stop on the tile the bomb exploded on. If players need to practice this, they are encouraged to try this on other monsters on a 4-tick attack cycle such as [[metal dragons]].

===Nylocas===
At the start of phase 2, Verzik will summon a group of nylocas who will home in on the player and self-destruct for up to 46 damage, or up to 8 if three tiles away from them. Players can safely "pop" them by letting them approach within three tiles, then running away from them. If they have not exploded after ~15 seconds of movement, they will die, making [[Ice Barrage]] a viable option to deal with them.

Additionally, a [[Nylocas Athanatos]] will also spawn, healing her for 9-10 health every few ticks. To kill the Athanatos, it has to be hit with poison or venom, which will cause it to absorb the poison and deal up to 70 damage on her.

After every third lightning ball, there is a 25% chance of the nylocas being summoned again. Should the summon trigger while the Athanatos is present, no nylocas will spawn.

===Phase 2.5===
When Verzik reaches 35.0% or less of her health, she will briefly stop attacking and summon two Nylocas Matomenos to her left and right. All players should swap to [[Protect from Magic]] during the transition. During the summoning animation, any damage dealt to her will heal her, so players should focus on the Matomenos until this animation ends.

She will also change up her attacks, now prioritising an AoE magic attack that targets a single player (and damages anyone in a 3x3 radius from them), dealing up to 45 damage and healing for 50% of the damage dealt.{{CiteTwitter|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1285291337621942274|author=Mod Ash|date=July 20 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/105626|archivedate=18 January 2022|quote=She's got a 75% chance of using a healing spell. It hits everyone near its target up to 45 (halved by prayer), counting the damage dealt, and then heals her for half of the total. So if she just hit 1 person for up to 45, and they prayed, that'd be ~22, healing her for 11.}} [[Protect from Magic]] will block the attack, but will still heal her for half the damage she would have dealt. Because of this, players should avoid standing next to each other when possible.

While the exploding nylocas and Athanatos will no longer be summoned for the remainder of the phase, she may still use her urnbomb and lightning attacks.

Make sure to heal to full before the next phase starts.

==Verzik Vitur - phase 3==
Verzik's chains break and she lands on the floor in a vampyre-nylocas form. Verzik will suffer a general combat drain during the transition, losing some Defence, Magic, and Ranged levels and bonuses in the process, though her melee accuracy will increase at the same time. Verzik will attack every 7 game ticks, and like in phase 2, will absorb any Defence-draining specials used against her.
[[File:Verzik Vitur - phase 3 tanking and popping.mp4|thumb|400px|The tank moves away from Verzik right before she attacks in order to prevent her from using melee. Meanwhile, the two other teammates successfully pop the two nylocas.]]

Unlike the previous phases, where Verzik frequently changes aggression, Verzik will pick one player in the team and pick them as their primary target for the duration of the phase. She will change aggro if her target does not stand within melee distance of her for more than 10 seconds. This timer will reset when the player is within melee distance of her. If a player is selected but is not experienced to tank, they should run away, or if a freezer is in the team, they may freeze her in place.

She can use all combat styles and her projectile attacks will hit all players in the room - stomping her front limbs launches ranged barbs, while crackling with blue energy will launch a blue orb magic attack, dealing up to 33 damage, reduced to 16 if prayed against. As her attacks are very accurate, it's important to switch prayers accordingly. Additionally, every attack, Verzik will check if her chosen target (the tank) is within melee distance or not. If they are, there is a chance for her to use a melee attack instead (which has a very similar animation to the magic attack, but a different sound played) that deals up to 63 damage on every player next to her that cannot be prayed against. This should be avoided at all times; regardless, players should keep their health above 80 to avoid being killed by this attack.

As such, the primary tank should either walk under or away from Verzik one or two ticks before she attacks to avoid the melee attack completely. Try to keep Verzik at the centre (phase start area) when possible. Moving away from Verzik will slightly displace her, but allows the base tank to react to attacks better. Moving under Verzik will keep her more grounded, but also means the base tank has less time to react to her attacks.

During this phase, Verzik has four special attacks that she uses in rotation, attacking '''four times''' before performing the next:
* '''Nylocas''' - identical to phase 2, but no Athanatos are ever summoned. Avoid dragging them into teammates, especially whoever is tanking. Freezing the nylocas will give the team more time to damage the boss.
* '''Sticky webs''' - Verzik moves to the centre of the room and launches webs towards players.
* '''Power blast''' - Verzik charges a powerful attack, where each player must stand on a different yellow pool that appears.
* '''Green ball''' - Verzik launches a green projectile to a player, requiring them to bounce it by being next to another player until it safely dissipates.

===Sticky webs===
Upon initiating this attack, Verzik will move towards to the centre of the room, becoming invulnerable in the process, until she begins launching webs. Any players in the area will be knocked away as she turns into a hard NPC (unable to be walked through) for the duration of this attack. She will then begin to launch webs at the players, three at a time if they are not on the same tile.

If a player is ensnared in a [[web (Verzik Vitur)|web]], they will be bound, requiring another player to free them by breaking the web, which has 10 Hitpoints. If not freed in time, the webs will snap and deal massive damage in the process. [[Aranea boots]] will negate the damage if caught in a web once every 8 ticks.

Experienced players can increase their DPS by following a clockwise rotation starting from the south, attacking once every 5 ticks. This requires immediately attacking Verzik after she is no longer invulnerable (spam click once in position), then running one-tick after the XP drop appears. When attacking in this manner, the players must attack on the '''same tick and tile'''. If this is not adhered to, lagging players will leave behind webs which may not despawn before the lead player(s) makes a full rotation, potentially causing them to be ensnared and take high damage as the web despawns. If a player is lagging behind, they must skip attacks until they catch up with the rest of the team to prevent this from occurring.

If players are unable to perform this method, they are recommended to break off and attack with ranged or magic until the mechanic ends.

<gallery mode="packed" heights="300" style="text-align:left">
Verzik Vitur - phase 3 web running.mp4|A demonstration of a perfect web run.
Verzik Vitur - phase 3 web fixing.mp4|In this demonstration, two players attacked Verzik one tick later, so they skip attacking one time in order to re-sync their attacks with the team.
</gallery>

===Power blast (yellows)===
[[File:Verzik Vitur - phase 3 yellow power blast tick eat.mp4|thumb|400px|To tick-eat the power blast, click on your food right as the projectile is directly above the player's head.]]
Upon initiating this attack, Verzik becomes invulnerable whilst charging up a powerful blast of energy. At the same time, yellow pools will appear to serve as protection from this attack. Each pool can only hold one player, so players should coordinate which pool they're going for to avoid confusion.

If the player is not on a pool before the shot hits, they will take up to 80 damage, which can be tick eaten. If several players stand on the same pool, they will all take damage while the pool fails to protect anyone, so try to avoid piling as this will result in unnecessary damage. Verzik is invulnerable while charging this attack, so use this time to restore health and stats as needed. There are 7 ticks between the end of this special attack and Verzik's next auto-attack. 

===Green ball===
As the last attack in her rotation, Verzik will launch a green ball at a random player, indicated by the game message {{mes|Verzik Vitur fires a powerful projectile in your direction...|colour=#0a721f}} Players can bounce the ball by being next to another player before impact, continuing to do so to a different player until it safely dissipates.

As it is difficult to coordinate bouncing the green ball - especially during the enrage phase - most teams will opt to simply take the hit, only bouncing it if its target is unable to survive the hit. If bouncing, the targeted player should follow another nearby player to ensure that it will bounce. The ball deals 75% of the player's [[Hitpoints]] level as damage (74 at level 99), so make sure to heal up before attempting to tank the ball. The ball can only be tick eaten if using a stall.

[[Redemption]] can also be used, but only if the player is going to have less than 10 health afterwards, as it can leave the player open to another attack with no prayer. A [[locator orb]] or [[dwarven rock cake]] may be used to trigger Redemption right before the ball hits, nulling the damage it would have dealt.

====Enrage phase====
[[File:Verzik Vitur - phase 3 webs enrage proc.mp4|thumb|400px|Experienced players with top-end gear may opt to proc the enrage phase mid-webs to end the raid quickly.]]
When Verzik reaches or falls below 20.0% of her hitpoints, she will yell {{overhead|I'm not finished with you just yet!}}, increasing the max hit of range/mage projectiles to 34 and summoning a purple tornado of fire for every player in the room; each one gets a personal tornado that tracks them down. If it makes contact with the player, they will take 50% of their current health as damage, while Verzik will heal for triple the damage dealt. Due to this, it is best to keep health around 50-60; it is more than enough to tank one off-prayer range or magic attack, and the tornado will only heal around 90 in the off chance it damages the player. Even one player getting hit for 57 (50% of 115) will cause Verzik to heal 171 health and will significantly set the team back. After a player is hit by their tornado, a new one will spawn 16 ticks later and begin following them again.

Additionally, her attack speed is increased from 7 (4.2 seconds) to 5 (3.0 seconds). The base tank should also take note of this to avoid killing other teammates with her melee attacks, and the increased attack speed will mean that special attacks are used more frequently. If the team's damage output is low, they may consider waiting until the power blast before triggering enrage, as it can be difficult to handle both mechanics at once. Teams with sufficient experience can simply power through into enrage; they can either keep their health low so the tornado heals little or try to enter the safe tile at the last possible moment, which is far riskier. The green ball attack should be tanked, or bounced if the targeted player doesn't have enough health to tank it; the other player will need to tank it in their place. Try to avoid targeting the base tank if bouncing is required, as the base tank is already pressured from Verzik's increased attack speed.

At this stage, players should dump all melee special attacks to end the phase as fast as possible.

Once Verzik is finally defeated her throne will collapse revealing a secret entrance to her treasure room, where players may collect their loot.

